# vector-unified — what git carries and what it deliberately does not.
#
# This repo was created 2026-07-25 to put 5,397 lines of previously UNVERSIONED
# pipeline code and its architecture docs under history. Before that, one
# accidental delete lost the joint-embedding work outright.
#
# Rule: source and docs are tracked; large GENERATED artifacts are not, because
# they are reproducible from the pipeline and would put ~43 MB of JSON blobs into
# history with no diffability. If you later want the published artifacts
# versioned, add git-lfs and un-ignore them deliberately — do not just delete
# these lines.

# Generated joint-embedding artifacts (assets/unified.json alone is 16.7 MB)
assets/*.json
assets/**/*.json
# ...and their TIMESTAMPED BACKUPS, which the two rules above miss. A file named
# `unified.json.pre_hoops_resync_20260731_063030` does not end in `.json`, so the ignore
# never applied and a 16 MB backup of a deliberately-ignored build output became the single
# largest tracked object in an 11 MB repo. The suffix convention is shared across this
# estate — vector-equities carries 18 of them (`.pre_*`, `.fixed_seed7_*`) — so match the
# pattern rather than the one file that happened to slip through.
assets/**/*.json.*
assets/**/*.npz.*
assets/**/*.pt.*

# Acquired + intermediate data (27 MB; re-fetchable via pipeline/acquire_*.py)
data/*
# EXCEPT the hand-authored anchors. These are SOURCE, not generated output, and both
# describe themselves as "version-controlled, changed only in a commit" — which was not
# true: `data/` swallowed them, `git add -A` skips ignored paths silently, and three
# commits reported shipping changes to archetype_map.json that never entered the repo.
!data/archetype_map.json
!data/sector_map.json
# Same category, same reason. Each entry is a HUMAN judgement that a superlative on a live
# page was checked against its artifact, with the evidence written down. Losing it on a
# fresh clone would not merely lose a report — every cleared claim reverts to UNCHECKED and
# check_superlatives.py --check fails for anyone but me. `git add -A` skips ignored paths
# SILENTLY, which is how archetype_map.json was reported as shipped in three commits it
# never entered; caught here only because git printed the hint.
!data/superlative_registry.json
# 40 hand-written cross-sport analogy pairs (Brady <-> Curry, Gobert <-> van Dijk). NO
# script writes this file — grep credited analogy_triples_eval.py, but that writes
# analogy_triples_REPORT.json. It is irreplaceable human work and was ignored until now,
# while two evaluators read it as a required input.
!data/analogy_triples.json
# Symbol-level dependency hashes. Losing these on a fresh clone would not lose a report --
# it would silently RE-ADD three permanent false STALE entries and send the next reader
# into 23 training runs they do not need.
!data/symbol_dep_registry.json
pipeline/data/

# Scraped-page cache — 11 spotrac_nfl_*.html files at ~2.6 MB each (~28 MB).
# Caught only by checking `git diff --cached` BEFORE the first commit: staging
# had ballooned to 581,559 lines. Scrape cache is re-fetchable and belongs
# nowhere near history.
pipeline/cache/
**/cache/

# A pre-pitch-consolidation backup copy of unified.json (16.7 MB duplicate)
pipeline/data/bak_pre_pitch_con/
**/bak_pre_*/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# transient logs from a detached ablation re-run
ablation_rerun.log
ablation_rerun.err
grl_seeds.log
grl_seeds.err
chain_ablation.ps1
grl_paired.log
coral_vicreg.log
chain_cv.ps1
